{"availability":"available","full":"Northbound-Dev/soroban-go-toolkit","name":"soroban-go-toolkit","description":"Soroban-go-toolkit is a lightweight Go client and CLI for interacting with Soroban smart contracts on Stellar. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-02T11:14:22Z","updated":"2026-10-09T19:15:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://soroban-go-toolkit.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://soroban-go-toolkit.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T20:53:01.844Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T20:53:01.844Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T20:53:01.844Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:07.305Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T20:53:01.844Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Go client library and CLI for reading Soroban smart contract state on the Stellar network.","Soroban tooling is concentrated in two ecosystems. Contract authors write Rust against rs-soroban-sdk, and frontends talk to the network through js-stellar-sdk and soroban-react.","Go is where a lot of backend infrastructure actually lives — indexers, bots, monitoring, internal services — and Go developers reaching for Soroban have had to hand-roll JSON-RPC calls and wrestle XDR themselves. The official stellar/go monorepo provides excellent XDR definitions and transaction building, but no dedicated Soroban RPC client."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Northbound-Dev/soroban-go-toolkit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1e6b965355b6de6a90161fbb6710ffef78260db17b004a283f3d88c274205686","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:07.435Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:07.435Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Go client library and CLI for reading Soroban smart contract state on the Stellar network.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Northbound-Dev/soroban-go-toolkit/blob/main/README.md"},"audience